  "MAEInfo": "Mean absolute error (MAE) is an average of absolute value of the residuals. Small MAE indicates that the model is well fitted to the training data",
  "R2Info": "Adjusted R2 takes value from 0 to 1, and high value indicates that the model is well fitted to the training data.\nGenerally, ordinal R2 improves by just adding new explanatory variables. Adjusted R2 is adjusted by the number of explanatory variables.",
